From: h713 <h713@local>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: h713-afbd: scan out NV12 directly

The CPU colour-conversion path costs 3.15 fps default and 14.93 fps with
videoconvert n-threads=4, because the decoder's CAPTURE buffers are uncached
CMA and reading them runs at ~44 MB/s. The GPU path avoids that entirely and
sustains 59.71 fps. This adds a third option that costs neither: let the
display fetch the decoder's NV12 and do the colour conversion at scanout,
which is what the vendor stack does -- "the vendor never reads the decoded
frame on the CPU".

THE REGISTERS ARE A SEPARATE PATH, not a mode of the existing one. AFBD_SRC
takes a single packed source and is the RGB path. NV12 needs a format selector,
both plane strides, both plane addresses, and an explicit publish:

  0x011  format   fmt_attr_tbl row index; 3 = 8-bit YUV420
  0x040  stride   luma bytes per line
  0x044  stride   chroma bytes per line
  0x070  address  Y plane, physical
  0x084  address  C plane, physical
  0x06c  dirty    write 1 to publish

WHY THIS WAS PREVIOUSLY THOUGHT IMPOSSIBLE, because the trail matters. The
2026-08-09 and 2026-08-12 attempts set the format byte and kept feeding
AFBD_SRC. The fetch therefore stayed 4 bytes/pixel and packed four source rows
into every display row -- the "4x repeat, greyscale" photographs. From that
null came the conclusion that this is a UI channel and Allwinner UI channels
are RGB-only, which was recorded at the time as an inference and later found
to be wrong: AFBD_PLANE_ADDR0/1 read zero throughout those runs and were
dismissed as "a parallel mechanism we do not use". They are the mechanism.
The addresses here come from the vendor's dec_reg_set_address() (base + 0x60,
index 0 at +16 and +36) and dec_reg_set_dirty().

The RGB path is left byte-for-byte as it was. The format selector is only
written when the format actually changes, and h->format is seeded at probe
with what U-Boot leaves running, so an RGB-only session issues exactly the
same register writes as before this patch.

NOT YET CONFIRMED ON HARDWARE at the time of writing: the individual registers
were verified to accept and retain values, and the sequence is the vendor's,
but the complete NV12 scanout has never been run. If it produces the 4x-repeat
signature again, the fetch is still packed and the format selector is not what
this patch assumes.


=======================================================================
REFUTED ON HARDWARE 2026-08-25. NOT IN series. KEPT FOR THE TRAIL.
=======================================================================

This patch is correct about everything except the one thing that matters:
the registers it writes are not in the scanout path.

Applied, built and booted. kmssink negotiated NV12 (it had failed to before),
and every value landed in hardware exactly as intended -- read back live while
a 1280x720 NV12 SMPTE source was streaming:

    0x05600011 = 0x03          format selector, NV12 row
    0x05600040 = 0x00000500    luma stride 1280
    0x05600044 = 0x00000500    chroma stride 1280
    0x05600070 = 0x77100000    Y plane
    0x05600084 = 0x771E1000    C plane   (C - Y = 0xE1000 = 1280*720 exactly)

The operator saw no colour bars. The panel still showed the login prompt.
Reading the channel-1 block that this driver actually scans out of, during the
same run, says why:

    0x05600170 = 0x00001400    stride 5120 = 1280 * 4 bytes/pixel
    0x05600178 = 0x76D00000    still the fbcon RGB framebuffer
    0x05600140 = 0x03001901    vendor RGB ctrl, untouched

The fetch never stopped being packed RGB from AFBD_SRC. The dirty latch at
0x0560006c read back 0.

CONCLUSION: 0x011/0x040/0x044/0x06c/0x070/0x084 are DECD's frame-submit
register file, driving a SEPARATE video plane. They are not a YUV mode of the
AFBD channel this driver flips. Writing them configures a plane that is not in
the active pipeline, which is why the sequence is inert rather than wrong.

This is the outcome video-decode.md predicted in its sequencing note -- "then
discover whether DECD can feed it at all given its registers are not in the
scanout path". That question now has an answer: it cannot, not without opening
the plane first.

Note what this does NOT refute. The register semantics recovered from the
vendor driver look right: the selector accepts 3, and the two plane addresses
are laid out exactly as NV12 requires. What is missing is the plane-open /
topology step, which the plane hunt established cannot be poked into a running
pipeline. Reviving this patch means doing that work first; on its own it only
adds a format that negotiates and shows nothing, which is a trap for the next
person, and is why it is out of series.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -67,6 +67,35 @@
 #define AFBD_STRIDE		0x170	/* bytes per line */
 #define AFBD_SRC		0x178	/* source physical address */
 
+/*
+ * The two-plane YUV path, which is a different set of registers rather than a
+ * variation on the one above. AFBD_SRC feeds a single packed source and is the
+ * RGB path; NV12 needs the format selector, both plane strides, both plane
+ * addresses, and an explicit publish.
+ *
+ * This is why the 2026-08-09 and 2026-08-12 attempts failed and why the
+ * "UI channels are RGB-only" conclusion drawn from them was wrong: they set the
+ * format byte and kept feeding AFBD_SRC, so the fetch stayed 4 bytes/pixel and
+ * packed four source rows into every display row. AFBD_PLANE_ADDR0/1 read zero
+ * throughout and were dismissed as a mechanism we did not use; they are the
+ * mechanism. Recovered from the vendor's dec_reg_set_address() (base + 0x60,
+ * index 0 at +16 and +36) and dec_reg_set_dirty().
+ */
+#define AFBD_FORMAT		0x011	/* byte: fmt_attr_tbl row index */
+#define AFBD_PLANE_STRIDE0	0x040	/* luma bytes per line */
+#define AFBD_PLANE_STRIDE1	0x044	/* chroma bytes per line */
+#define AFBD_DIRTY		0x06c	/* write 1 to publish the config */
+#define AFBD_PLANE_ADDR0	0x070	/* Y plane physical address */
+#define AFBD_PLANE_ADDR1	0x084	/* C plane physical address */
+
+/*
+ * fmt_attr_tbl row indices, not DEC_FORMAT_* ids. Row 0 is what the live path
+ * U-Boot leaves running reads as; the vendor writes 6 and 7 for 10-bit YUV420
+ * and AV1, which puts 8-bit NV12 at row 3.
+ */
+#define AFBD_FMT_RGB888		0
+#define AFBD_FMT_NV12		3
+
 #define AFBD_IRQ_VSYNC		BIT(0)
 #define AFBD_STATUS_DONE	BIT(1)
 
@@ -79,6 +108,7 @@
 	struct clk *clk_bus;
 	struct drm_display_mode mode;
 	unsigned int stride;
+	u32 format;		/* last DRM fourcc programmed */
 };
 
 static inline struct h713_afbd *to_h713(struct drm_device *drm)
@@ -91,17 +121,49 @@
  * gles-play's commit path, minus its 50 ms poll for STATUS_DONE: here the
  * vblank interrupt reports completion, so nothing spins.
  */
-static void h713_afbd_set_source(struct h713_afbd *h, dma_addr_t addr,
-				 unsigned int stride)
+static void h713_afbd_set_source(struct h713_afbd *h,
+				 struct drm_plane_state *state)
 {
+	struct drm_framebuffer *fb = state->fb;
 	u32 pending;
 
-	if (stride != h->stride) {
-		writel(stride, h->regs + AFBD_STRIDE);
-		h->stride = stride;
-	}
+	if (fb->format->format == DRM_FORMAT_NV12) {
+		dma_addr_t y = drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(fb, state, 0);
+		dma_addr_t c = drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(fb, state, 1);
+
+		if (h->format != DRM_FORMAT_NV12) {
+			writeb(AFBD_FMT_NV12, h->regs + AFBD_FORMAT);
+			h->format = DRM_FORMAT_NV12;
+			/* Force the RGB stride to be rewritten on the way back. */
+			h->stride = 0;
+		}
+
+		writel(fb->pitches[0], h->regs + AFBD_PLANE_STRIDE0);
+		writel(fb->pitches[1], h->regs + AFBD_PLANE_STRIDE1);
+		writel(lower_32_bits(y), h->regs + AFBD_PLANE_ADDR0);
+		writel(lower_32_bits(c), h->regs + AFBD_PLANE_ADDR1);
+		writel(1, h->regs + AFBD_DIRTY);
+	} else {
+		unsigned int stride = fb->pitches[0];
 
-	writel(lower_32_bits(addr), h->regs + AFBD_SRC);
+		/*
+		 * Only touched when coming back from NV12. U-Boot leaves the
+		 * selector on the RGB row, so the packed path stays exactly as
+		 * it was before this register was known about.
+		 */
+		if (h->format != fb->format->format) {
+			writeb(AFBD_FMT_RGB888, h->regs + AFBD_FORMAT);
+			h->format = fb->format->format;
+		}
+
+		if (stride != h->stride) {
+			writel(stride, h->regs + AFBD_STRIDE);
+			h->stride = stride;
+		}
+
+		writel(lower_32_bits(drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(fb, state, 0)),
+		       h->regs + AFBD_SRC);
+	}
 
 	pending = readl(h->regs + AFBD_STATUS);
 	if (pending)
@@ -122,10 +184,7 @@
 	 * buffer the client handed us so the first commit is not a no-op.
 	 */
 	if (plane_state->fb)
-		h713_afbd_set_source(h,
-				     drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(plane_state->fb,
-							     plane_state, 0),
-				     plane_state->fb->pitches[0]);
+		h713_afbd_set_source(h, plane_state);
 
 	drm_crtc_vblank_on(&pipe->crtc);
 }
@@ -150,9 +209,7 @@
 	unsigned long flags;
 
 	if (state->fb)
-		h713_afbd_set_source(h,
-				     drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(state->fb, state, 0),
-				     state->fb->pitches[0]);
+		h713_afbd_set_source(h, state);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&crtc->dev->event_lock, flags);
 	event = crtc->state->event;
@@ -256,6 +313,12 @@
 static const u32 h713_afbd_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
+	/*
+	 * Two-plane YUV straight off the decoder: no colour conversion on the
+	 * CPU and none on the GPU, which is how the vendor stack drives this
+	 * display. See AFBD_PLANE_ADDR0/1 above.
+	 */
+	DRM_FORMAT_NV12,
 };
 
 /*
@@ -280,6 +343,9 @@
 	}
 
 	h->stride = readl(h->regs + AFBD_STRIDE);
+	/* U-Boot leaves the packed RGB path running; match it so the first
+	 * RGB commit does not rewrite a selector that is already correct. */
+	h->format = DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888;
 	drm_info(drm, "adopting %ux%u, stride %u, source %08x\n",
 		 w, hgt, h->stride, readl(h->regs + AFBD_SRC));
 
